ged**\n- **`src/attr/_compat.py`**: added `_IS_GENERATOR_RESULTS` and `_lazy_is_generator`. The answer is cached on first call, and unhashable callables get the uncached answer.\n- **`src/attr/_make.py`**: the generated `__setattr__` runs a generator hook in three steps. It sets the first yielded value, then resumes the generator. A second yield closes it and raises `RuntimeError`. Plain hooks and hookless names behave as before. Also added the `attrib` `versionchanged` note.\n- **`src/attr/_next_gen.py`**: the `define` and `field` docstrings describe generator hooks and carry the `26.2.0` notes.\n- **`src/attr/setters.py`**: `pipe` has the warning that generators aren't allowed. Its behaviour is unchanged.\n- **`src/attrs/__init__.pyi`**: `_OnSetAttrType` also accepts a generator-returning callable.\n- **`docs/examples.md`**: new section \"Running Custom Code Before/After Setting Attributes\" with the doctest example. I ran that example separately and its output matches the spec.\n\n**Deviations**\n- The spec names `_ClassBuilder._make_own_setattr`, but this repo calls the method `add_setattr`. I made the change there.\n- I did not change `docs/examples.md` beyond the new section. The Markdown doctest is not run by the spec's check.\n\n**Lint**\n- `ruff format` is clean on the files I touched.\n- `ruff check` reports one error, RUF063 at `src/attr/_compat.py:35`. That line is existing code I did not touch.", "ttft_ms": 1327, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 62622, "uuid": "b2af5238-fedf-445f-bda9-d3248f6f6a28", "ttft_stream_ms": 1046, "time_to_request_ms": 346, "first_content_frame_ms": 1046, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
